cluster-judge.instruction:
Read docs/TASK_PHASE7.md FIRST -- sections 2.2 and 3.2, which is your acceptance -- and the four examples of Function Recheck Watchlist in the cluster group of contour.yaml. ethsc/cluster.py is in your context: read it, do not modify it. You patch only tests/test_cluster_examples.py. Keep all eight existing tests exactly as they are.

Add one test per new contour example, four in all:
(a) the store from codes_26077729.json with the seed 0xb4e16d0168e52d35cacd2c6185b44281ec28c9dc labelled "UniV2 pair seed" gives exactly 4 alerts -- 0x22052a1a..., 0x2621cc0b... and 0x3041cbd3... with 1.0, then 0xcf6daab9... with 26/32 -- and the seed's own address is not among them;
(b) the same store with min_score=1.0 gives only the three 1.0 alerts, and with seed_addresses=[the seed address in UPPER case] gives the same list as the default call;
(c) a store holding code_belle.hex at 0x34c6211621f2763c60eb007dc2ae91090a2d22f6 and its four code_belle_copy_*.hex at 0x1807090dd15a6f58e00fd769e32ebf20ee610385, 0x2141be5f2afa674c94167ab167a478a56cb539f5, 0x46cadea509dc3d3c96a11fb61ab8b222f5238f0a and 0x6411bed82614b91ef655d82486e0bd3a13d2eb8c, seeded "BELLE honeypot", gives the same 4 alerts twice in a row, each score 13/15, in that address order;
(d) that store with no seeds gives [], and with seed_addresses=["0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111"] gives [] as well.

Your tests are the judge, so they compare the exact list, not a length: a mutation check runs them against a recheck_watchlist that keeps the seed's own address and sorts by score only, and at least two of your tests must go red on it. Set maxDiff = None on your class so a failing comparison prints the difference.

Use the loaders already in the file (_block_store, _read_hex, _temp_db) and do NOT import tests.helpers -- the acceptance rejects it. Every assert needs msg=. Do not touch any other file.

